  "thesis": "Up 31.5%, then down two days running: by Wednesday midday NVDA had given back about half of its comeback rally, and Congress is lining up hearings.",
  "lede": "NVIDIA's board unanimously reinstated Jensen Huang as President, CEO and director on Nov 23, citing input from senior levels of the US government. NVDA closed Monday at $165.05, up 31.5%; it fell 5.9% Tuesday to $155.38 and was down another 7.2% at $144.21 at 12:36 PM ET Wednesday, about 15.5% below Monday's close, as hot inflation data and new tariff plans hit chips worldwide. In 390 verified quotes from 237 voices, opposition outnumbers support about two to one. No member of Congress on record supports the move; on Wednesday Sen. Cory Booker wrote to board chair Harvey Jones asking whether NVIDIA is \"too big to hold accountable.\" The administration doubled down: Trump said a pardon is \"always an option.\" In Taiwan, the public mood is warmer: most people quoted on the street and online welcomed him back. Huang faces a closed House Intelligence session on Dec 1 and a public Senate Banking hearing on Dec 3.",
